==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈtɪlə/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tiller.wav |Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪlə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|tilier}}; equivalent to {{suffix|en|till|er}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A person who [[till]]s; a [[farmer]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2000|author={{w|Alasdair Gray}}|title=The Book of Prefaces|page=63|publisher=Bloomsbury|year_published=2002
|passage=In France, Europe's most fertile and cultivated land, the '''tillers''' of it suffered more and more hunger.}}
# A machine that mechanically tills the soil.

